From: so1_sanctum <so1_sanctum@pm.me>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 10:42:02 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] ptlc: monitor believes only accepted unlocks, unlock keeps a
 margin, Ed25519 locks are checked

ptlc.monitor printed the first Unlock, ProxyUnlock or Reclaim of an entry it
found on the contract's chain, accepted or not. Anyone can send a refused
unlock with a junk witness ahead of the real one, and a counterparty reading
that would add the tweak to junk and miss its own claim. It now reports
refused calls as refused, keeps watching, and checks the accepted witness
against the lock before printing it.

ptlc.unlock and ptlc.proxyUnlock judged expiry by the machine's clock and sent
with any time left. They now read the frontier momentum and refuse with under
60 s: an unlock answered after the expiry is refused with its witness public.

ptlc.create refuses an Ed25519 lock that is no point, or a point of small
order, which the contract accepts and anyone can open.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
